Experiment 6 – Step-by-Step Procedure
Title: Automate Test Runs Using GitHub Actions
Step 1: Open Repository
Open GitHub⁠�.
Log in to your account.
Open your GitExperiment1 repository.
Step 2: Create Python Test File
Click Code.
Click Add file → Create new file.
Enter the filename test_math.py.
Type the Python test code:
def test_addition():
    assert 2 + 3 == 5

def test_subtraction():
    assert 5 - 2 == 3

def test_multiplication():
    assert 4 * 3 == 12
Step 3: Save the Test File
Click Commit changes.
Enter the commit message Add Python test cases.
Select Commit directly to the main branch.
Click Commit changes.
Step 4: Create Workflow File
Open the .github folder.
Open the workflows folder.
Click Add file → Create new file.
Enter the filename test.yml.
Step 5: Write Workflow Configuration
Paste the following YAML code into the editor:
name: Run Tests

on:
  push:
    branches: ["main"]
  pull_request:
    branches: ["main"]

jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v4
        with:
          python-version: "3.x"

      - name: Install pytest
        run: |
          python -m pip install --upgrade pip
          pip install pytest

      - name: Run tests
        run: pytest
Step 6: Save the Workflow File
Click Commit changes.
Enter the commit message Add automated Python test workflow.
Select Commit directly to the main branch.
Click Commit changes.
Step 7: Open GitHub Actions
Open the repository.
Click the Actions tab.
Select Run Tests on the left side.
Click the latest workflow run.
Step 8: Verify Test Results
Click the test job.
Open the Run tests step.
Check whether the output shows that all three tests passed.
Expected result: 3 passed with a green tick (✓).
Step 9: Result
The Python test cases were automatically executed using GitHub Actions, and all three tests passed successfully.
